# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# .planning/ alone is ~3,600 files and ~900 PNGs of design evidence. Shipping
# it to the daemon on every build costs seconds and megabytes for material the
# image never reads — and it is also where household-identifying material
# lives, which has no business inside a published container.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.hermes
.planning
docs
node_modules
dist
test-results
playwright-report
.playwright
tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.mjs
*.sqlite*
__pycache__
**/*.py

# Local compose state and secrets: an .env copied into the image would bake
# one household's credentials into a distributable artifact.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
README.md
PRE-PUBLICATION.md
LICENSE
